fp|p|at|A B C|fp||
at|^^^c@2In the |cp|gr|at|^*b Button Area^*n,|cp||at| which is just above the chapter column (left), are the three letter button icons  { A } { B } { C } .
You can |cp|a|at|^*bhover^*n|cp||at| over any of them to see its Tooltip,       (|cp|a|at|^*bTry It^*n|cp||at|). 
|n^|5|at|
Each of the letter buttons lets you save a different size and layout (position of the two divider bars) in the ^*b aaBridge ^*n window.
|n^|5|at|
In addition, you can ^*b optionally ^*n save the POSITION of the ^*b aaBridge ^*n window.  

|n^|1|fp|e-37|at|How to Use|fp||at|^c@2
|n#|3|at|To  SAVE  the current aaBridge window |fp|e-37|at|^*b size ^*n|fp||at| and |fp|e-37|at|^*b layout ^*n|fp||at| 
|n#|1|cp|a|at|^*bhold down ^*n|cp||at| the  |fp|e-37|at|^*b Ctrl ^*n|fp||at|  key and keep it held down  ^*b WHILE ^*n you click on  { A } , { B }  or  { C } . 

|n^|3|at|To ^*b also ^*n SAVE  the current aaBridge window |fp|e-37|at|^*b position|fp||at|
|n#|1|cp|a|at|^*b hold down ^*n|cp||at| ^*bboth^*n|at|  the |fp|e-37|at|^*b Alt ^*n|fp||at| and the |fp|e-37|at|^*b Ctrl ^*n|fp||at| key and keep them held down ^*b WHILE ^*n you click the letter button. 

|n^|3|at|A |cp|a|at|^*b simple click ^*n|cp||at| of the chosen button restores whatever you have saved,     (|cp|a|at|^*bTry It^*n|cp||at|).|

