qx|Fit|
mn|    Lines  Don't  Fit     |
n^|7|
lg|c|
at|^c@2At the time of writing, early 2025, a number of new Java implementations are available, e.g. your computer has an ARM cpu. These new Java's can have slightly larger fonts that the older common Oracle Java 8 (aka 1.8).  These larger fonts, especially on Linux, can cause lines that SHOULD fit across the normal aaBridge page not to fit and so spill over onto the following line, so forcing text further down the page.|
at|^^^^|
fp|p|at|^bThe Fix|fp||
at|^^The ^*b Font Shrink ^*n setting (see just under the LOWER divider, then on the right) allows you to make your fonts slightly smaller.  But do not expect that setting  'good values'  will fix ALL layout issues.  Some old lin files in this collection were not that good in the first place ?
^^|n^|g|at|
There is also a ^*b Main Panel Width ^*n adjuster  just below  'Font Shrink'  but this has far less effect.
^^|

lg||n#|3|fp|t|at|^bGRID|fp||lg|c|at|
When using ^*b Font Shrink ^*n  best to have the GRID showing, see the^*b next page^*n of this lin file.
Ideally the bottom left hand corner of the GRID should display as shown below.|
n#|7|
lg||at|@0@1

line 33
line 34
|cp|Dgray|at|         < - - - blank line, last line on page|cp||
n^|q|cp|green|at|^*b^c zone z^*c|cp||




